From: Ivory <contact@ivory.cafe>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 12:27:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Confine synchronous output preparation to minimum storage
 authority

Define the helper domain, executable label, private property type, and descriptor-transfer permissions needed for fixed owner-user external-storage traversal.

Constraint: system_server must not gain external-storage open, read, write, or create permissions
Rejected: DAC_OVERRIDE, DAC_READ_SEARCH, or permissive policy | each would broaden the root helper beyond the fixed preparation protocol
Confidence: high
Scope-risk: moderate
Directive: Keep system_server limited to fuse directory ioctl for O_PATH receipt and preserve helper regular-file denial
Tested: selinux_policy including neverallow, compatibility, freeze, and context tests; enforcing-device run with no feature AVC
Not-tested: full user image build is outside the agreed acceptance scope
Change-Id: Id9a7fd2fa074983a6aa9d33351671f5a7c78fc9d
